# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit the filled copy.
#
# Config is read ONCE at startup through a single validated module. A missing value
# fails the process loudly at boot rather than defaulting to something plausible —
# the previous build defaulted a missing key and ran for seven hours doing nothing.

# ── database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One Postgres, three schemas: public (what the app may read), internal (decisions,
# labels, features — the app has NO grant here), raw (vendor captures).
#
# The values below are the LOCAL-DEV-ONLY credentials from docker-compose.yml, so
# `pnpm db:up && pnpm db:migrate && pnpm db:seed` works on a fresh clone with
# nothing to fill in. They are worthless outside that container. Replace all of
# them for anything that is not your laptop.
#
# Owner. Runs the migrations and, locally, stands in for the service and internal
# roles — those are NOLOGIN group roles created by migration 0001 and have no
# password to put here.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://insidor:insidor@127.0.0.1:5432/insidor
# Separate role for the app. Read-only, public schema only. This is the second half
# of "the app cannot show internal scoring" — the first half is the wire types.
#
# ★ RUN THE READ SERVICE AS THIS ONE EVEN LOCALLY. `insidor_app_user` is granted
# insidor_app and nothing else, so it has SELECT on six public tables plus the
# projection, no USAGE on internal or raw, and no grant on public.observation. A
# query that would leak gets "permission denied" from Postgres instead of
# rendering. Running it as the owner locally leaves that untested everywhere
# except production. `pnpm db:migrate` creates this user.
DATABASE_URL_APP=postgresql://insidor_app_user:insidor_app@127.0.0.1:5432/insidor
# store/src/client.ts picks the connection string by role and refuses to fall back
# to another role's credentials, so the projector needs its own name for the owner
# URL above. It must NOT be a transaction-mode pooler (port 6543): that releases
# session advisory locks between statements and withAdvisoryLock would silently
# stop guarding anything. client.ts throws rather than let that happen.
DATABASE_URL_SERVICE=postgresql://insidor:insidor@127.0.0.1:5432/insidor
DATABASE_URL_INTERNAL=postgresql://insidor:insidor@127.0.0.1:5432/insidor

# ── social sources ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reddit. FREE — no card, no plan, no per-post billing, unlike the two below.
#
# Get these at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> "create app":
#   name          anything (insidor-dev)
#   type          script          <- must be "script", not "web app"
#   redirect uri  http://localhost
# The client id is the short string under the app name; the secret is labelled.
#
# A script app authenticates as YOUR account, so treat the secret like a password:
# it belongs in .env.local (gitignored) and nowhere else — not in a commit, not in
# a screenshot, not pasted into a chat window.
#
# The grant is client_credentials — the app id and the app secret, and NOTHING else.
# A script app is a confidential client, which is exactly who that grant is for, so no
# Reddit account password is needed or wanted anywhere in this repository. Anything
# asking for one is asking for more than the adapter needs.
#
# Reddit REQUIRES a descriptive User-Agent and bans generic ones — its own rule is
# "NEVER lie about your user-agent", and a default library string is throttled into a
# shared bucket. The shape below is theirs; fill in a real username, because the point
# of the field is that they can contact whoever is running the client. The adapter
# REFUSES TO CONSTRUCT with the placeholder still in it, with a browser or library name
# in it, or with no /u/ contact — see adapters/platform/reddit/src/client.ts.
#
# Theirs is the only free tier here with a documented rate limit, so calls still go
# through the meter at zero cost: billed 'per-call', because the request is the unit
# actually being rationed. An unmetered free source is how a free source quietly
# becomes a blocked one.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=script:com.insidor.adapter:v0.1.0 (by /u/YOUR_REDDIT_USERNAME)

# X via reseller. Billed per post returned, so every call passes through the meter.
#
# One value turns this source on: a single API key, sent as an X-API-Key header. There
# is no OAuth, no token to refresh and no account password wanted anywhere in this
# repository — anything asking for one is asking for more than the adapter needs.
#
# ★ THE KEY MUST NOT CARRY WHITESPACE, and the adapter REFUSES TO CONSTRUCT if it does
# rather than sending it. A value pasted with a trailing newline is the ordinary way
# that happens, and a newline inside a header value means the request that goes out is
# not the request the code wrote. It fails at boot, naming this variable, instead of as
# a 401 that sends somebody to re-issue a key that was fine.
#
# ★ AND NOTE HOW THIS ONE BILLS: per post returned, WITH A MINIMUM OF ONE POST PER
# REQUEST — a call that returns nothing still costs. That is why the ledger books a
# whole unit for an empty page rather than zero, and why nothing in the adapter retries:
# a retry here is a second real charge.
X_API_KEY=
# The reseller host. Not a credential, so it has a default in code
# (adapters/platform/x/src/credentials.ts) and leaving this blank is fine.
X_API_BASE=https://api.twitterapi.io

# TikTok via scraper. Note it cannot be used for a blind historical run, and the reason
# is not that no date filter exists — one scraper family does document an upload-date
# bound. It is that the candidate set is chosen by a PRESENT-DAY RANKING before any date
# filter is applied, so filtering it afterwards makes a contaminated selection LOOK
# blind; and which actor is configured, hence whether such a filter is honoured at all,
# is not knowable to our code. The adapter refuses the query — see
# adapters/platform/tiktok/src/discover.ts.
#
# ★ THIS SOURCE NEEDS FOUR VALUES, NOT ONE, AND THE OTHER THREE USED TO BE MISSING
# FROM THIS FILE ENTIRELY. Supplying only the token produced a client that constructed
# happily and could not run anything — the worst of the three states, because it looks
# configured. Now the shortfall is answered at boot, by name, as a MISCONFIGURED
# reading: somebody turned this on and got it wrong, which is a fault, and is
# deliberately not the same reading as the source nobody turned on.
#
# The actor ids identify which third-party scraper we run. They are configuration
# rather than constants because swapping to a cheaper or re-published actor is a
# commercial decision with a price attached, and none of those is a deploy of this
# repository. There is no default for either: we have no id we could honestly default
# to, and a plausible wrong one is worse than an absence.
#
# ★ WRITE AN ACTOR ID IN ITS API FORM: "username~actor-name", with a TILDE, or the bare
# generated id. The platform's console shows the same actor as "username/actor-name",
# and pasting THAT form here would add a segment to the request path — a request that is
# valid, wrong, and answered with a 404 that reads exactly like a retired actor. The
# adapter REFUSES TO CONSTRUCT on the slash form and tells you which spelling to use.
#
# ★ AND NOTE HOW THIS ONE BILLS: per RUN. A run that finds nothing costs the same as one
# that finds a thousand posts, and a run we start and walk away from keeps billing —
# which is why the adapter hands the platform an explicit run timeout rather than hoping.
APIFY_TOKEN=
TIKTOK_DISCOVERY_ACTOR_ID=
TIKTOK_OBSERVE_ACTOR_ID=
# The scraper platform's public host. Not a credential, so it has a default in code
# (adapters/platform/tiktok/src/credentials.ts) and leaving this blank is fine.
TIKTOK_API_BASE=

# ★ LEAVING ANY OF THESE BLOCKS EMPTY IS A SUPPORTED, PERMANENT STATE. A source with
# no credential is DORMANT: the process boots, the loops run, the board renders, and
# the indicator says which sources are off. It is NOT an error and nothing retries it.
# Filling one in is the only thing needed to turn that source on — no code change, no
# migration, one restart. Emptying it again turns it off just as cleanly.
#
# The one state that IS a fault is a HALF-filled block, because that is somebody
# believing a source is running when it is not. It reads as FAILING, beside the
# variable that is missing, rather than as "you have not turned this on".

# ── chain and market ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The mint stream. One long-lived websocket, its own process (services/chainwatch).
PUMPPORTAL_WS=wss://pumpportal.fun/api/data
# RPC for confirming mint times. Every outcome label hangs on this being right.
SOLANA_RPC_URL=
HELIUS_API_KEY=

# ── judge ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only where a trained model does not exist yet. Bounded by a hard daily cap:
# when the cap is hit the stage PAUSES rather than quietly running up a bill.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5

# ── embeddings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Grouping needs real sentence embeddings. The previous build used bag-of-words word
# counting under the name "embeddings", which is why 91% of its stories held a single
# post by a single author.
EMBEDDING_API_KEY=

# ── the mint watcher (services/chainwatch) ───────────────────────────────────
# One long-lived process, one durable cursor, one coverage log. It is a separate
# deployable from the runner because every runner deploy restarts the runner, and
# a restart mid-cursor is a hole in the coverage log.
HEALTH_PORT=8081
SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS=20000
SINGLETON_LOCK_NAME=insidor.chainwatch
MINT_FEED_ID=solana-mints
MINT_FEED_CHAIN=solana
# The transport is a DECLARATION, not a switch — nothing in the supervision
# branches on it. It is here so the log line and the port tell the truth about
# what is running.
MINT_FEED_TRANSPORT=stream
# The drain cadence. Low, because a push transport is only as live as the rate we
# empty its buffer.
POLL_INTERVAL_MS=3000
PAGE_LIMIT=500
# ★ The width of a silence we call jitter rather than a hole. Every lead-time
# number the product publishes is computed over windows this defines, so there is
# no default for it anywhere. Must be greater than POLL_INTERVAL_MS.
COVERAGE_TOLERANCE_MS=15000
# Where the push transport connects. Named for what it is, not for who runs it —
# the vendor name must never reach a service, a payload or a rendered string.
MINT_STREAM_URL=wss://pumpportal.fun/api/data
# Bounded on purpose: an unbounded queue is an out-of-memory crash during a mint
# storm, and a crash is a gap nobody chose the shape of. Overflow is DECLARED as
# a coverage gap instead. Must be at least PAGE_LIMIT.
MINT_STREAM_BUFFER_LIMIT=5000
# A nominally-connected socket that delivers nothing for this long is treated as
# dead. This is the half-open socket: TCP alive, no bytes, no close event, every
# liveness check answering yes. Must be greater than POLL_INTERVAL_MS.
MINT_STREAM_STALE_MS=90000
# ★ The second honesty number. How many seconds before a notification reached us
# the mint is allowed to have happened. A socket event is an UPPER BOUND on the
# mint, never the mint time, so this is what makes it comparable at all — the
# stored instant is centred (observed - lag/2) with a half-width of lag/2.
MINT_OBSERVATION_LAG_S=10
BACKOFF_BASE_MS=1000
BACKOFF_MAX_MS=60000
HEARTBEAT=off

# ── discovery (services/runner) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Whether the runner goes looking for new items at all.
#
# ★ IT HAS TO BE DECLARED, exactly like HEARTBEAT above and for the same reason. A
# defaulted-off discovery is a pipeline that runs, reports healthy and ingests nothing
# — the seven-hour silent failure this whole service is shaped around. Silence is
# chosen, never inherited.
#
# ★ AND IT IS NOT THE SAME QUESTION AS "WHICH SOURCES ARE LIVE". That is answered by
# the credential blocks above and by nothing else. This switch decides whether we ask
# ANY of them; merging the two would make turning discovery off for an afternoon
# indistinguishable from losing every credential.
DISCOVER=off
# What to look for, comma separated. Required when DISCOVER=on, and an empty list is
# refused rather than treated as off: a discovery loop with nothing to look for runs,
# reports success, and ingests nothing.
DISCOVER_TERMS=

# ── runtime ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
